  "body": "## What was wrong\n\nEvery fallback on the routing page has ↑/↓ arrows. The primary model above them did not — so the arrows stopped exactly at the entry that actually serves the traffic. Promoting a fallback meant retyping two fields by hand and hoping they agreed.\n\nA route *is* one ordered path: `MODEL` plus the comma-joined chain beside it. It just happens to be stored as two settings.\n\n## What this does\n\nThe rail reorders as the single list it looks like. The primary gets the same two buttons every row under it has, wired to the `ModelChainEditor` next to it — that class already owns the ordering rules, so nothing new decides what \"up\" means.\n\nAll six rails share one builder (`appendRouteRail`): the four tier overrides, the default route, and the vision adapter. A rail that reorders differently from the one beside it reads as a bug, not as a distinction.\n\n```\n1  nvidia_nim/nemotron-3   [↑ off] [↓ on ]        <- primary (MODEL)\n2  groq/llama-3.3-70b      [↑ on ] [↓ on ] [x]\n3  cerebras/qwen-3-480b    [↑ on ] [↓ off] [x]\n\npress ↓ on row 1 ->\n\n1  groq/llama-3.3-70b      <- MODEL\n2  nvidia_nim/nemotron-3   <- MODEL_FALLBACKS[0]\n3  cerebras/qwen-3-480b\n```\n\n## Why it is a swap and never an insert\n\nNo button press can leave a route without a primary. Both halves of that matter and they fail differently:\n\n- **An empty `MODEL` fails validation**, so the server refuses to start. Loud, recoverable by hand.\n- **An empty tier override is quiet and worse.** Routing reads a route's own fallbacks only when that route has its own primary, so clearing `MODEL_OPUS` silently orphans `MODEL_OPUS_FALLBACKS` — the tier drops back to the root model *and* the root chain, with nothing in the log to say the chain next to it stopped being consulted.\n\nSo demotion is gated on there being a fallback to swap with, and re-gates live as the primary is typed in. **Promotion deliberately is not gated that way**: promoting into an unset override is exactly how a route stops inheriting the default, and there the row is removed rather than left holding an empty value.\n\nThat orphan behaviour is now **pinned in `test_routing_chains.py`** rather than left as a comment, so nobody \"fixes\" the button gate into a bug.\n\n## Verification\n\nDriven in **jsdom against a real running server** (throwaway `HOME`, port 8147), 29 assertions, all passing — including a demote/promote round trip leaving both hidden inputs byte-identical to where they started, and `changedValues()` carrying both settings so Apply writes them together.\n\nPositive control, same harness against unmodified `main`:\n\n```\nport 8148 (main)    rails: 6   primary move clusters: 0\nport 8147 (branch)  rails: 6   primary move clusters: 6\n```\n\nOn `main` the harness cannot even reach its first assertion — the buttons do not exist.\n\nGuards mutation-tested, each failing **by name**:\n\n| mutation | caught by |\n| --- | --- |\n| M1 a bespoke rail built outside `appendRouteRail` | `reorders_a_route_rail_as_one_list` |\n| M2 `setPrimary` wiring dropped (dead arrows) | `reorders_a_route_rail_as_one_list` |\n| M3 demote gate relaxed to allow an empty primary | `never_lets_a_button_empty_a_route_primary` |\n| M4 promote gate tightened (unset stays unset) | `never_lets_a_button_empty_a_route_primary` |\n| M5 down button stops honouring the gate | `never_lets_a_button_empty_a_route_primary` |\n| M6 the new CSS block lost in a merge | `styles_every_class_the_script_emits` |\n| M7 routing merges an orphaned chain | `orphaned_when_its_override_is_cleared` |\n\nLocal CI: `ruff format --check`, `ruff check` and `ty` all clean; pytest **4795 passed, 26 skipped**, with the documented **6 `test_install_ps1_*` checksum failures** that are the standing local baseline on this machine (they fail identically on unmodified `main` and never run on Linux CI).\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- **The \"Custom route\" / \"Inherits default\" chip does not update live.** It is computed at render, so filling a previously unset override by promotion leaves the chip reading \"Inherits default\" until the next load. Pre-existing — typing in the field does the same — and deliberately out of scope.\n- **Not seen in a real browser.** jsdom has no layout engine, so the button alignment is reasoned from the DOM (a hidden copy of the remove button holds the column) and from the CSS, not measured. That is the one thing worth a second pass.\n- Unrelated, found while measuring and **not touched**: `BRAVE_EXTRA_SNIPPETS` is a boolean whose payload `value` is `\"\"` while its checkbox reads `false`, so it sits in `changedValues()` on a freshly loaded page — on `main` too. It rides along on the next unrelated Apply.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
